messages:
hana_dx: Customer onboarding hit a wall deploying our JS SDK to Deno Deploy and Bun. Minimal import causes runtime failures.

hana_dx: Repro they shared:
```ts
import { createClient } from '@redwood-inference/sdk';
const c = createClient({ apiKey: Deno.env.get('REDWOOD_KEY') });
await c.ping();
```
Errors: Deno -> "ReferenceError: process is not defined" and "TypeError: globalThis.crypto.subtle is not a function". Bun -> "Failed to resolve specifier \"node:crypto\"" or sometimes hits CJS path.

leo_sdk: thanks. TL;DR our package mixes node: prefixed imports and Node-only globals. Edge runtimes either don't provide those or forbid specifiers.

leo_sdk: immediate customer workaround for Deno: prepend a tiny shim file that sets process.env and a webcrypto fallback, e.g.
```ts
// deno/shim.ts
(globalThis as any).process = { env: { REDWOOD_KEY: Deno.env.get('REDWOOD_KEY') } };
if (!globalThis.crypto) { (globalThis as any).crypto = { getRandomValues: (u: Uint8Array) => { throw new Error('no crypto available') } } }
```
Import the shim before the SDK. Not ideal but unblocks them.

tia_build: long term we should ship an explicit ESM edge build that avoids node: imports and uses webcrypto-compatible APIs. Proposal: add `dist/edge.mjs` and a package export subpath `@redwood-inference/sdk/edge` or `./edge` in package.json.

tia_build: crypto adapter sketch:
```ts
export async function randomBytes(n:number){
  if (typeof globalThis.crypto?.getRandomValues === 'function'){
    const a = new Uint8Array(n); globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues(a); return a;
  }
  const cr = await import('crypto');
  return cr.randomBytes(n);
}
```
Dynamic import avoids static `node:` resolution in the edge build. Ensure bundler keeps the dynamic import only in node-targeted builds.

omar_infra: Bun quirks: Bun sometimes resolves conditional exports to the wrong entry (CJS require). Make the deno/bun entry explicit in exports to ensure `import '@redwood-inference/sdk/edge'` picks the neutral ESM build. Also doc the bun CLI flags if needed.

leo_sdk: Types: customers using Deno complain about mismatched fetch/RequestInit types. Quick wins: add `examples/deno/tsconfig.json` recommending `lib: ["dom","esnext"]`, and publish a `types-deno.d.ts` with small compatibility defs. Longer: use `typesVersions` to map to Deno-friendly types.

hana_dx: they also asked about streaming support in Workers/Bun. We should document what the edge entrypoint supports (no Node ReadableStream; prefer WHATWG streams or chunked JSON).

leo_sdk: plan: 1) Add `edge` build target in tsup/rollup, 2) add `./edge` export, 3) add examples for Deno and Bun with import_map and tsconfig, 4) docs page "Using SDK in Deno/Bun/Workers" with shims and streaming notes, 5) add CI smoke tests (lightweight) running the examples.

ci-bot: created issue RED-4120: "JS SDK: Deno/Bun edge entry + shims + types + CI" assigned to @leo_sdk.

hana_dx: thanks team. I'll pass the shim + ETA to the customer and link the examples when the PR lands. :thumbsup:
